# Production build config (`npm run build`). Vite loads this — and NOT
# .env.local — for the `production` mode, so it wins for the shipped bundle.
#
# Empty (but SET) VITE_API_URL → the app calls the API at same-origin relative
# paths (/chat, /alerts, …). That's exactly right when the built bundle is
# served by the API itself: `python -m src serve` mounts frontend/dist/ at / and
# answers /chat on the same origin. No CORS, no second port, one process.
#
# (An UNSET VITE_API_URL would instead force mock mode — see src/api/client.ts.)
VITE_API_URL=
